WEBVTT

00:00:00.930 --> 00:00:06.100
<b><i>Chihayafuru 3</i></b>

00:00:06.100 --> 00:00:07.930
<b><i>Chihayafuru 3</i></b>

00:01:10.000 --> 00:01:15.010
Verse 5

00:01:10.000 --> 00:01:15.010
Mount 
Amanokagu

00:01:15.040 --> 00:01:17.420
<i>She's closed the gap from 
three cards to one.</i>

00:01:17.420 --> 00:01:19.480
<i>That high school girl's 
putting up a good fight!</i>

00:01:20.000 --> 00:01:22.280
<i>It'll all depend on which cards are read.</i>

00:01:22.280 --> 00:01:24.820
<i>Inokuma-san's plenty fast at taking cards, too.</i>

00:01:25.210 --> 00:01:27.600
This is the biggest battle 
of speed we've had today.

00:01:25.230 --> 00:01:28.230
Yoshino\h\h\h
 Tournament

00:01:25.230 --> 00:01:28.230
Quarterfinals

00:01:31.470 --> 00:01:33.550
<i>The reason this is such a close match now</i>

00:01:33.550 --> 00:01:36.960
<i>is because Haruka-san was rattled 
when she lost "Impassionate."</i>

00:01:37.700 --> 00:01:38.660
<i>the red that is the Tatsuta River</i>

00:01:38.740 --> 00:01:40.070
<i>the red that is the Tatsuta River</i>

00:01:45.090 --> 00:01:47.590
<i>She's having fun playing.</i>

00:01:48.190 --> 00:01:49.930
<i>I can't let her get into a groove.</i>

00:01:49.930 --> 00:01:53.760
<i>I need to throw off her pace 
and not let her have fun!</i>

00:01:56.940 --> 00:01:58.500
Hey! Aki!

00:02:05.080 --> 00:02:07.630
<i>That logo on his chest! It's Daddy Bear!</i>

00:02:07.630 --> 00:02:09.340
If you can't be quiet, we're leaving, Aki.

00:02:09.340 --> 00:02:09.900
No!

00:02:09.900 --> 00:02:13.110
Mommy's game looks fun! No! I wanna watch!

00:02:10.900 --> 00:02:12.890
I'm sorry. I'm so sorry.

00:02:13.110 --> 00:02:15.470
<i>Yay! Another fellow Daddy Bear fan!</i>

00:02:18.140 --> 00:02:20.690
<i>My parents were karuta players, too.</i>

00:02:18.650 --> 00:02:21.240
<i>now white robes hang to 
dry on Mount Amanokagu</i>

00:02:21.030 --> 00:02:24.340
<i>I spent more weekends at their 
practice hall than anywhere else.</i>

00:02:25.260 --> 00:02:29.860
<i>Then I won the Queen title four times
and had two adorable kids.</i>

00:02:30.580 --> 00:02:32.850
<i>I should be able to say that's enough...</i>

00:02:39.500 --> 00:02:44.740
<i>But the realization that parents 
can have something they treasure</i>

00:02:44.740 --> 00:02:46.620
<i>as much as their kids set me free.</i>

00:02:47.830 --> 00:02:50.150
<i>My children will grow up.</i>

00:02:50.150 --> 00:02:52.180
<i>That's why I have to shine in karuta.</i>

00:02:52.990 --> 00:02:56.180
<i>My karuta is a kind of karuta</i>

00:02:58.230 --> 00:03:00.020
<i>that I enjoy more than anyone else!</i>

00:03:00.770 --> 00:03:08.940
<i>May the scarlet kadsuras of Mount 
Afusaka live up to their name</i>

00:03:09.510 --> 00:03:11.630
<i>"May my sighs" is on her side,</i>

00:03:11.630 --> 00:03:14.610
<i>but she went for "May the scarlet" on 
her opponent's side after one syllable.</i>

00:03:15.030 --> 00:03:16.640
<i>That only makes sense.</i>

00:03:16.950 --> 00:03:19.720
<i>Ayase was targeting the opponent's side.
She wouldn't get back in time.</i>

00:03:21.660 --> 00:03:22.650
<i>No...</i>

00:03:23.230 --> 00:03:25.530
<i>It's not that Inokuma-san 
was playing offensively.</i>

00:03:27.490 --> 00:03:28.810
<i>She knew!</i>

00:03:30.320 --> 00:03:31.840
<i>That's a given.</i>

00:03:31.840 --> 00:03:34.130
<i>Haruka-san was born in Yamaguchi,</i>

00:03:34.130 --> 00:03:36.480
<i>so she excels when the reader
is from the west.</i>

00:03:37.250 --> 00:03:39.500
<i>She can discern the subtle 
differences in intonation.</i>

00:03:40.800 --> 00:03:42.920
<i>She just takes them because she can hear.</i>

00:03:42.920 --> 00:03:45.370
<i>That's a Queen's game sense.</i>

00:03:46.720 --> 00:03:48.170
<i>She's back.</i>

00:03:48.390 --> 00:03:51.280
<i>Right down to that childish smile...</i>

00:03:57.780 --> 00:04:05.330
<i>and allow us this secret rendezvous</i>

00:04:07.310 --> 00:04:14.810
<i>Would the mountain cherry 
blossoms return my affection,</i>

00:04:08.770 --> 00:04:09.870
Dead card!

00:04:09.870 --> 00:04:11.300
<i>But "Would this" moved!</i>

00:04:11.300 --> 00:04:12.050
<i>That's a fault!</i>

00:04:12.550 --> 00:04:14.820
<i>Which one touched it?!</i>

00:04:19.060 --> 00:04:20.750
That was just a blow by, right?

00:04:34.500 --> 00:04:35.950
Wow, really?

00:04:37.330 --> 00:04:41.180
<i>I felt no stiffness at all
in her shoulder back then.</i>

00:04:43.090 --> 00:04:46.550
<i>I thought she'd tense up
 against a former Queen,</i>

00:04:46.950 --> 00:04:49.190
<i>but right from the start,
and even this close to the end,</i>

00:04:49.190 --> 00:04:51.120
<i>she's not getting worked up.</i>

00:04:54.820 --> 00:04:57.570
<i>Maybe in Ayase's mind, the only Queen...</i>

00:04:58.700 --> 00:05:01.140
<i>is Wakamiya Shinobu.</i>

00:05:03.800 --> 00:05:05.620
<i>No matter how strong she is...</i>

00:05:15.910 --> 00:05:18.250
<i>Shinobu-chan is even stronger!</i>

00:05:19.710 --> 00:05:23.620
<i>She's playing an unrestrained game,
even in such an intense back-and-forth.</i>

00:05:23.940 --> 00:05:28.360
<i>This is such a seesaw battle! As a veteran,
Inokuma-san may be used to it...</i>

00:05:28.360 --> 00:05:30.360
<i>...but she's just a high schooler!</i>

00:05:34.840 --> 00:05:39.880
<i>Her faith in Wakamiya's strength 
is keeping her relaxed.</i>

00:05:41.470 --> 00:05:42.140
<i>But...</i>

00:05:47.940 --> 00:05:50.540
<i>Even Wakamiya Shinobu isn't invincible.</i>

00:06:01.100 --> 00:06:02.940
<i>Faith?</i>

00:06:05.010 --> 00:06:06.310
Thank you very much.

00:06:06.460 --> 00:06:08.170
Thank you very much.

00:06:08.480 --> 00:06:09.830
Yes!

00:06:09.830 --> 00:06:11.440
<i>What?!</i>

00:06:11.440 --> 00:06:12.960
<i>Hiroshi-kun won!</i>

00:06:12.960 --> 00:06:14.050
<i>Coach Tsuboguchi!</i>

00:06:14.060 --> 00:06:16.060
<b>Shock</b>

00:06:14.060 --> 00:06:16.060
The Nagumo
 Society's hopes 
were so 
high, they're
 stunned silent

00:06:16.600 --> 00:06:19.090
<i>Those last five cards in a row...</i>

00:06:19.090 --> 00:06:21.820
<i>They were exactly the 
ones he was aiming for.</i>

00:06:21.810 --> 00:06:27.320
<b>You're going to win</b>

00:06:22.200 --> 00:06:24.010
<i>Was it some kind of curse?</i>

00:06:31.000 --> 00:06:32.930
<i>Arata lost...</i>

00:06:32.930 --> 00:06:34.570
<i>Even Arata...</i>

00:06:35.480 --> 00:06:36.590
<i>This is why...</i>

00:06:40.530 --> 00:06:42.310
<i>...karuta is so unpredictable.</i>

00:06:47.660 --> 00:06:55.720
<i>Impassioned vows exchanged over 
many a tear shed to last</i>

00:06:49.170 --> 00:06:51.180
<i>until the day waves crash 
over Mount Suenomatsu</i>

00:06:56.180 --> 00:06:58.190
Thank you very much.

00:06:58.380 --> 00:07:00.310
Thank you very much.

00:07:01.170 --> 00:07:02.700
<i>Dr. Harada...</i>

00:07:03.010 --> 00:07:04.760
<i>Murao-san won?</i>

00:07:05.180 --> 00:07:09.440
<i>Heh! That Harada's wiped 
out after five matches!</i>

00:07:07.690 --> 00:07:09.450
<b>Pathetic</b>

00:07:09.790 --> 00:07:11.820
Well done, Murao-kun!

00:07:11.820 --> 00:07:15.320
But his ten-card lead in the middle
was knocked down to four.

00:07:16.300 --> 00:07:18.880
That took a lot out of Murao-kun.

00:07:19.230 --> 00:07:30.170
<i>Damn it! Damn it! Damn it! Damn it!</i>

00:07:24.210 --> 00:07:27.280
<i>That'll affect him later.</i>

00:07:27.280 --> 00:07:30.170
<i>This is why karuta is so scary...</i>

00:07:34.400 --> 00:07:35.950
<i>Four cards left...</i>

00:07:36.750 --> 00:07:38.760
<i>They both have two.</i>

00:07:39.330 --> 00:07:40.500
<i>They're even.</i>

00:07:42.260 --> 00:07:43.780
<i>How will this end?</i>

00:07:45.270 --> 00:07:46.400
<i>How will it end?</i>

00:07:46.400 --> 00:07:47.280
<i>How is this going to end?!</i>

00:07:49.120 --> 00:07:50.020
<i>How will it end?</i>

00:07:54.270 --> 00:07:55.330
<i>That's not it!</i>

00:07:55.330 --> 00:07:57.210
<i>Keep attacking until the end and win it!</i>

00:07:55.950 --> 00:08:02.440
<i>Said bed was cold as I lay awake</i>

00:07:58.910 --> 00:08:02.450
<i>They both gambled and went for
the opponent's side at this late stage!</i>

00:08:02.450 --> 00:08:04.780
<i>Could these Shiranami Society 
people be any more reckless?!</i>

00:08:04.780 --> 00:08:07.660
<i>What the hell is he even teaching them?!</i>

00:08:10.580 --> 00:08:12.560
<i>Whether they win or lose...</i>

00:08:12.560 --> 00:08:14.190
<i>They give us strength.</i>

00:08:17.920 --> 00:08:20.690
<i>It was partly because
she had an aggressive mindset,</i>

00:08:19.750 --> 00:08:29.000
<i>for the night would drag on 
when I thought of my beloved</i>

00:08:21.040 --> 00:08:22.440
<i>but the way Ayase's taking cards...</i>

00:08:31.710 --> 00:08:39.440
<i>Since I could not hide my love,</i>

00:08:34.530 --> 00:08:35.490
<i>people would always ask if 
I was pining for someone</i>

00:08:45.510 --> 00:08:47.180
Thank you very much.

00:08:48.130 --> 00:08:49.740
Thank you very much.

00:08:50.500 --> 00:08:52.190
Sh-She fell aslee—

00:08:52.190 --> 00:08:53.390
B-But she won!

00:08:53.390 --> 00:08:57.630
Wake up, Chihaya-chan! You won!

00:08:59.180 --> 00:09:00.640
<i>Ayase's grabs</i>

00:09:00.640 --> 00:09:04.730
<i>people would always ask if 
I was pining for someone</i>

00:09:02.180 --> 00:09:04.020
<i>are starting to go silent.</i>

00:09:08.090 --> 00:09:09.060
<i>Prez!</i>

00:09:09.060 --> 00:09:09.860
<i>Mashima!</i>

00:09:11.060 --> 00:09:14.620
<i>I-It's luck of the draw!</i>

00:09:11.860 --> 00:09:14.610
<b>Again!!</b>

00:09:14.850 --> 00:09:18.940
<i>Why are all these fools
so pointlessly persistent?</i>

00:09:18.940 --> 00:09:21.620
<i>I'll show you how good my luck is!</i>

00:09:27.530 --> 00:09:29.010
<i>Luck of the draw...</i>

00:09:27.960 --> 00:09:30.630
<i>are joined at river's end</i>

00:09:31.840 --> 00:09:33.260
<i>Luck of the draw...</i>

00:09:33.260 --> 00:09:41.680
<i>people would always ask if 
I was pining for someone</i>

00:09:42.390 --> 00:09:42.510
<i>are joined at river's end</i>

00:09:42.960 --> 00:09:49.960
<i>Like the sound of someone 
knocking on my door,</i>

00:09:46.840 --> 00:09:48.750
<i>He went straight for the opponent's side?!</i>

00:09:51.930 --> 00:09:59.900
<i>the thistle and brush are 
blown by the autumn wind</i>

00:09:55.580 --> 00:09:57.370
Thank you very much.

00:09:57.840 --> 00:09:59.580
Thank you very much.

00:10:00.230 --> 00:10:03.630
Damn you! What kind of 
karuta are you playing?!

00:10:03.630 --> 00:10:06.130
Don't take risks like 
that out of desperation!

00:10:09.080 --> 00:10:11.420
At this point,

00:10:12.440 --> 00:10:15.840
I'm not so optimistic as to think
the card on my side will be read again.

00:10:17.850 --> 00:10:20.440
What the hell? That's just creepy!

00:10:22.940 --> 00:10:24.260
<i>This is why...</i>

00:10:25.160 --> 00:10:26.920
<i>karuta is so fun!</i>

00:10:28.600 --> 00:10:31.460
Fantastic, Chitose-chan!

00:10:31.460 --> 00:10:33.170
Let's see more of the bag.

00:10:34.020 --> 00:10:35.940
Now turn your head the other way.

00:10:35.940 --> 00:10:37.480
Yes, that's it!

00:10:38.020 --> 00:10:40.630
Okay, let's take a break. Go on and change.

00:10:40.630 --> 00:10:42.400
Thank you.

00:10:43.190 --> 00:10:44.210
Oh, Mom!

00:10:44.210 --> 00:10:45.880
I brought your phone.

00:10:45.880 --> 00:10:48.990
Thanks! I couldn't believe I forgot it!

00:10:48.990 --> 00:10:51.740
I had to slip out of work for you, you know?

00:10:51.740 --> 00:10:54.370
You could've just had Chihaya bring it.

00:10:54.370 --> 00:10:56.990
No, she's at a tournament today.

00:10:56.990 --> 00:10:58.460
Oh, shoot! My break's over!

00:10:58.750 --> 00:11:00.150
They'll take this out of my pay!

00:11:01.470 --> 00:11:04.750
I'm sorry I haven't earned 
as much as I hoped to.

00:11:04.750 --> 00:11:06.760
I just keep racking up costs for lessons...

00:11:06.760 --> 00:11:07.460
Huh?

00:11:10.110 --> 00:11:11.220
It's all right.

00:11:11.530 --> 00:11:13.780
I like my part-time job at the supermarket,

00:11:13.780 --> 00:11:16.530
and Chihaya's karuta doesn't cost that much.

00:11:18.030 --> 00:11:20.490
<b>Stored Fare Used</b>

00:11:18.030 --> 00:11:20.490
<b>Balance</b>

00:11:18.030 --> 00:11:20.490
Tap IC Card

00:11:18.170 --> 00:11:20.020
<i>Other than the hakama, anyway.</i>

00:11:21.850 --> 00:11:23.990
<i>I'll barely make it for the timed sale...</i>

00:11:29.300 --> 00:11:31.000
Oh... I'm sorry.

00:11:34.460 --> 00:11:35.960
I'm heading out!

00:11:37.530 --> 00:11:39.790
<i>I hope Chihaya gave it her best.</i>

00:11:41.260 --> 00:11:44.590
<i>I hope that hakama we bought in 
twelve installments is all right.</i>

00:11:46.090 --> 00:11:48.560
Chihaya-chan, wake up!

00:11:48.560 --> 00:11:49.600
Ayase!

00:11:49.600 --> 00:11:51.550
You won, so you have another match to play!

00:11:51.550 --> 00:11:53.600
We will now decide the semifinal match-ups.

00:11:53.600 --> 00:11:58.110
Tsuboguchi Hiroshi   Murao Shinichi
 Ayase Chihaya         Mashima Taichi

00:11:54.670 --> 00:11:56.320
And there it is!

00:11:56.320 --> 00:11:58.110
Ayase's playing Hiroshi-san next!

00:11:59.940 --> 00:12:01.700
<b>Victory</b>

00:12:02.280 --> 00:12:05.200
Excuse me. I'd like to yield the match.

00:12:05.640 --> 00:12:07.320
I'll take the loss by default.

00:12:07.320 --> 00:12:09.820
What?! Coach, you're taking a loss?!

00:12:07.330 --> 00:12:15.580
"Yield" 

00:12:07.330 --> 00:12:15.580
Often used when a 
player is matched 
with a member of 
the same society, 
or when it's late
and a player might
miss their ride home

00:12:09.080 --> 00:12:15.580
<b>This is
common</b>

00:12:10.370 --> 00:12:12.020
Oh, all right.

00:12:11.710 --> 00:12:15.580
<b>Used to it</b>

00:12:12.020 --> 00:12:15.020
We'll only have one Class A
semifinal match, then.

00:12:16.250 --> 00:12:18.950
Just let Chihaya-chan sleep.

00:12:20.150 --> 00:12:21.590
You worked hard.

00:12:22.340 --> 00:12:24.000
Tsuboguchi-san...

00:12:33.140 --> 00:12:34.300
Having a rough time?

00:12:35.500 --> 00:12:38.120
But this is it, Eyelashes!

00:12:39.680 --> 00:12:45.760
Most people here think you're just a kid 
who rode a wave of momentum to get here.

00:12:46.280 --> 00:12:48.510
You're playing a high 
schooler in the semifinal?

00:12:48.510 --> 00:12:50.540
Good thing it's not Tsuboguchi-kun.

00:12:50.540 --> 00:12:53.020
Oh, I'm sure Murao-kun can handle it.

00:12:53.020 --> 00:12:55.790
But the members of our society know...

00:12:56.500 --> 00:12:59.540
that you don't have much momentum or luck.

00:12:58.290 --> 00:12:58.540
<b>Huh?!</b>

00:12:58.540 --> 00:12:59.550
<b>Huh?!

00:13:00.420 --> 00:13:01.730
What you have is skill.

00:13:03.050 --> 00:13:05.900
Go out there and show that
your skill's what got you here!

00:13:08.390 --> 00:13:09.540
<i>Hiroshi-san...</i>

00:13:10.530 --> 00:13:12.990
<i>Don't say scary stuff like that.</i>

00:13:14.550 --> 00:13:18.260
<i>If it turns out that
I don't actually have the skill...</i>

00:13:20.880 --> 00:13:22.920
<i>Murao-san is an older member 
of Arata's society.</i>

00:13:23.530 --> 00:13:25.270
<i>There's no doubt he's good.</i>

00:13:30.850 --> 00:13:34.000
I stole them.

00:13:37.950 --> 00:13:39.250
<i>Arata...</i>

00:13:40.500 --> 00:13:41.520
<i>is watching.</i>

00:13:43.180 --> 00:13:44.720
Sakurazawa-san!

00:13:45.850 --> 00:13:47.150
Haruka-san.

00:13:47.590 --> 00:13:50.120
Great playing today. Heading home?

00:13:50.120 --> 00:13:52.510
I need to get home and make dinner.

00:13:52.510 --> 00:13:54.220
And there's laundry too, right?

00:13:55.690 --> 00:13:59.570
Sakurazawa-san, why don't you give 
me your current contact info?

00:14:01.240 --> 00:14:03.860
I'd like you to practice with me.

00:14:05.360 --> 00:14:08.060
I'll take better care of my contacts.

00:14:08.060 --> 00:14:10.210
These glasses just aren't working out.

00:14:10.210 --> 00:14:14.090
I do have children, so it 
won't be easy to make time,

00:14:14.740 --> 00:14:18.460
but I've had enough of losing 
before I've given my all.

00:14:21.760 --> 00:14:24.730
Losing "Impassionate" really 
affected you, didn't it?

00:14:29.840 --> 00:14:31.410
With her fourth consecutive win,

00:14:31.410 --> 00:14:33.390
Queen Chihara Haruka!

00:14:36.450 --> 00:14:39.740
I'm Inokuma Haruka now!

00:14:49.940 --> 00:14:53.570
When fast players start to lose their speed,

00:14:53.570 --> 00:14:55.850
they get fed up and quit.

00:14:57.270 --> 00:14:59.010
That's what happened to me.

00:14:59.550 --> 00:15:03.320
I've had enough of losing 
before I've given my all.

00:15:10.180 --> 00:15:14.180
Ayase Chihaya

00:15:10.180 --> 00:15:14.180
Murao Shinichi

00:15:10.180 --> 00:15:14.180
Mashima Taichi

00:15:11.140 --> 00:15:14.190
You seem awfully relaxed, Hiroshi-kun.

00:15:14.550 --> 00:15:16.880
You mean because I yielded to Chihaya-chan?

00:15:17.370 --> 00:15:19.790
But wouldn't you have done the same thing?

00:15:20.140 --> 00:15:21.920
The real battle is in two weeks.

00:15:21.920 --> 00:15:24.430
I'm not young anymore.

00:15:25.440 --> 00:15:28.110
If they'll give me a serious match,

00:15:28.110 --> 00:15:31.860
I'll play like my life depends on it, 
even against a favorite student.

00:15:32.580 --> 00:15:35.220
Because I might still have room to grow.

00:15:35.220 --> 00:15:38.570
Before I play against the Master...

00:15:38.570 --> 00:15:40.770
I can still...

00:15:47.730 --> 00:15:49.220
Damn it...

00:15:49.220 --> 00:15:53.640
That means nothing if I'm here
losing to Murao-kun.

00:15:53.830 --> 00:15:56.740
We're having a review meeting when this 
is over! You and me, Hiroshi-kun!

00:15:56.740 --> 00:15:57.370
Huh?!

00:15:57.370 --> 00:15:58.850
Shut up! You're joining me!

00:16:02.700 --> 00:16:03.880
Hiroshi-kun...

00:16:04.360 --> 00:16:08.910
If you had been matched with Eyelashes,
would you have yielded?

00:16:11.510 --> 00:16:13.150
<i>...show that your skill's what got you here!</i>

00:16:15.650 --> 00:16:18.230
Well, actually...

00:16:19.610 --> 00:16:21.750
I think I would've tried to crush him.

00:16:23.130 --> 00:16:27.050
I would've been as stubborn 
as I was with Wataya-kun.

00:16:29.240 --> 00:16:31.910
<i>This is my first time watching Taichi play.</i>

00:16:32.650 --> 00:16:34.270
<i>He was the biggest surprise of all,</i>

00:16:34.700 --> 00:16:38.000
<i>sticking with karuta and 
even making Class A.</i>

00:16:38.550 --> 00:16:41.600
I actually have a life, so I can't
spend all my time playing karuta,

00:16:41.600 --> 00:16:43.940
but I'll be better than you in no time!

00:16:45.800 --> 00:16:47.950
What's the deal, Arata-kun? 
You're being a bit creepy.

00:16:48.520 --> 00:16:49.740
It's time.

00:16:50.600 --> 00:16:52.140
The match will now begin.

00:16:52.770 --> 00:17:00.190
<i>Naniwa Bay, now the flower 
blooms, but for winter</i>

00:17:00.680 --> 00:17:05.360
<i>Confirm... Confirm... Confirm...</i>

00:17:02.130 --> 00:17:09.010
<i>Here comes spring, 
now the flower blooms</i>

00:17:04.120 --> 00:17:06.580
<i>makes me wonder how I ever 
let you fade from my mind</i>

00:17:05.830 --> 00:17:08.390
One point... One point...

00:17:08.860 --> 00:17:10.180
<i>That one point...</i>

00:17:10.740 --> 00:17:12.520
<i>"Like a" hasn't come up yet.</i>

00:17:12.520 --> 00:17:14.180
<i>Be careful of "Like the."</i>

00:17:14.510 --> 00:17:16.740
<i>Inokuma-san wouldn't mistake them.</i>

00:17:16.740 --> 00:17:18.890
<i>But make sure to take "Since I."</i>

00:17:18.890 --> 00:17:21.340
<i>Take it as soon as I hear the S sound.</i>

00:17:18.930 --> 00:17:20.720
<i>people would always ask if 
I was pining for someone</i>

00:17:22.140 --> 00:17:24.490
<i>Your class trip is in Kyoto?</i>

00:17:24.490 --> 00:17:26.090
<i>That's perfect.</i>

00:17:26.910 --> 00:17:29.500
<i>Let's pway in the Queen match together...</i>

00:17:30.360 --> 00:17:32.070
<b>Swish                     Swish</b>

00:17:30.590 --> 00:17:32.070
<i>in costumes!</i>

00:17:32.070 --> 00:17:33.690
In costumes?!

00:17:33.690 --> 00:17:36.670
Wh-Wh-Wh-What were you dreaming 
about, Chihaya-chan?!

00:17:37.150 --> 00:17:38.070
Dreaming?

00:17:38.070 --> 00:17:39.850
You've been asleep all this time.

00:17:40.200 --> 00:17:41.850
What is this wet spot?!

00:17:41.850 --> 00:17:43.610
Th-That's drool, I think...

00:17:43.610 --> 00:17:44.630
Drool?!

00:17:44.630 --> 00:17:46.530
No! Don't rub it!

00:17:46.120 --> 00:17:53.880
<b>Drool</b>

00:17:46.540 --> 00:17:49.270
B-B-But Kana-chan! My kimono!

00:17:49.270 --> 00:17:51.900
It's all right! We can get it out for you!

00:17:51.900 --> 00:17:53.030
Will it come out?!

00:17:53.030 --> 00:17:53.880
Yes, it will!

00:17:55.340 --> 00:17:57.590
I'm sorry, Mom...

00:17:57.590 --> 00:17:59.260
Mom...

00:18:03.090 --> 00:18:06.760
We have some time. Why don't 
I straighten your kimono for you?

00:18:07.800 --> 00:18:11.800
Chihaya-chan, you should've had your 
mom come here to cheer you on.

00:18:11.800 --> 00:18:13.950
She should see you in your brand-new kimono.

00:18:13.950 --> 00:18:17.530
Yeah, but she works part-time until evening.

00:18:17.530 --> 00:18:20.160
My grandpa out in the country isn't well.

00:18:20.160 --> 00:18:22.720
He always says, "I have diabetes 
and all kinds of things,"

00:18:21.410 --> 00:18:24.790
I have diabetes and all kinds of things

00:18:22.720 --> 00:18:25.380
so she sends him money for 
hospital stays and caregiving.

00:18:25.380 --> 00:18:28.050
And she did buy this hakama for me.

00:18:29.890 --> 00:18:33.290
My sister asks our mom for 
stuff all the time, but...

00:18:37.320 --> 00:18:38.430
Wait...

00:18:38.430 --> 00:18:40.380
Come to think of it,

00:18:40.840 --> 00:18:41.920
what about my match?

00:18:58.530 --> 00:19:00.700
<i>I can't believe Murao-kun</i>

00:19:01.140 --> 00:19:04.700
<i>is down by five cards. 
If something doesn't change...</i>

00:19:07.210 --> 00:19:08.440
<i>Murao-san...</i>

00:19:10.790 --> 00:19:11.770
<i>Yes!</i>

00:19:11.770 --> 00:19:12.300
<i>That's it.</i>

00:19:12.850 --> 00:19:14.540
<i>Be aggressive, Murao-san.</i>

00:19:15.500 --> 00:19:19.540
<i>His simpleminded aggressiveness is 
Murao-kun's strongest asset in karuta.</i>

00:19:20.320 --> 00:19:23.800
<i>He focuses intently on discerning sounds
and attacks single-mindedly.</i>

00:19:25.230 --> 00:19:29.750
<i>And I've also been teaching Eyelashes to play
offensive karuta in the Shiranami Society.</i>

00:19:34.310 --> 00:19:35.400
<i>But...</i>

00:19:37.200 --> 00:19:39.150
<i>What is that timing?</i>

00:19:40.230 --> 00:19:42.060
<i>That slight delay</i>

00:19:43.770 --> 00:19:45.930
<i>turns into the perfect defense.</i>

00:19:49.850 --> 00:19:51.580
<i>Should I test it?</i>

00:19:53.240 --> 00:19:54.520
<i>Can I do it?</i>

00:19:57.960 --> 00:19:59.280
<i>He did it!</i>

00:19:59.280 --> 00:20:03.980
<i>He leaned his whole body forward and turned 
only his arm the other way for a pull-back!</i>

00:20:05.470 --> 00:20:07.860
<i>I can't pull off an attack.</i>

00:20:08.210 --> 00:20:11.480
<i>How is Mashima playing so freely?</i>

00:20:12.970 --> 00:20:14.620
<i>Chihaya isn't here.</i>

00:20:15.370 --> 00:20:16.820
<i>Arata is watching.</i>

00:20:17.420 --> 00:20:18.470
<i>And...</i>

00:20:19.450 --> 00:20:21.740
<i>Dr. Harada is weighing him down.</i>

00:20:32.500 --> 00:20:34.530
<i>There's no way Murao-san will lose.</i>

00:20:38.190 --> 00:20:39.550
<i>There's no way.</i>

00:20:41.100 --> 00:20:44.810
<i>Maybe the best way Eyelashes 
can improve is actually...</i>

00:20:50.840 --> 00:20:53.090
<i>with defensive karuta!</i>

00:20:54.840 --> 00:20:56.560
Thank you very much.

00:20:56.970 --> 00:20:58.830
Thank you very much.

00:21:25.640 --> 00:21:26.930
<i>The final is...</i>
